Description: CCS desktop application (GTK) for several Claude Code accounts
 The "CCS" GTK application of ccs: accounts and usage, Claude Code chat,
 files and roadmap of each project, history, analysis, settings, and the
 top bar indicator. It can also drive the projects of a CCS server (VPS).

Package: ccs-serveur
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ccs (= ${binary:Version}),
         python3-aiohttp,
         python3-pyotp,
         python3-qrcode,
         libpam0g,
         adduser,
         systemd
Description: CCS server: drive Claude Code from a browser, phone or terminal
 Runs CCS on a server (VPS): a web interface (responsive, for phones) and an
 API for the desktop application and `ccs tui`. Users log in with their
 Ubuntu account (PAM, members of the "ccs" group, never root) and a
 mandatory TOTP code. Services: ccs-auth (root, minimal), ccs-web
 (unprivileged, 127.0.0.1:8420, behind a reverse proxy) and one bridge per
 logged-in user.

Package: ccs-all
Section: metapackages
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ccs (= ${binary:Version}),
         ccs-bureau (= ${binary:Version}),
         ccs-serveur (= ${binary:Version})
Description: CCS, complete: command line, desktop application and server
 Metapackage that installs the three CCS packages at once: ccs (command line,
 usage service, `ccs tui`), ccs-bureau (GTK application) and ccs-serveur (web
 interface and API, Ubuntu accounts and TOTP login).
